Subject: [PATCH 134/155] rule-set: a local list in the format text is read;
 due rule-sets download five at a time

The case of the format text in the reload of a local rule-set lost the default
branch after it, so a local list in that format was refused as of an unknown
format; remote lists were not touched. A test reads one now.

The updater downloaded the rule-sets that were due one after another. Since a
rule-set with nothing cached may start empty, the first downloads of all of
them are the updater's, and on a router without a cache on flash that is every
list after every reboot. Due rule-sets are now downloaded together, as many at
a time as the start downloads (five); each is touched by one goroutine, and what
they came to is counted after.
